<<~ ahu #/rank-1-live-equivocation>>

!! RANK 1 — The live-equivocation recovery gap (the hardest open exposure)

The field's verdict is unanimous and it CONFIRMS our honesty: ''no deployed or researched system recovers from a fully live key capture using key material alone.'' Every real mechanism does one of four things, and the residual — an attacker holding current + successor material simultaneously (or a full threshold within one epoch) who ''acts inside the window'' — is unsolved everywhere.

''VINDICATION (our exposure is real, universal, and correctly framed).''

* KERI states it outright: ''"there is no recovery mechanism once the keys for the root control authority have been fully captured"'' (https://trustoverip.github.io/kswg-keri-specification/). Pre-rotation defends only the ''next'' rotation, exactly as our `nextHandleKeyDigest` does — it cannot touch a simultaneous current+next seizure. KERI superseding-rule A1 (''a non-delegated rotation cannot supersede another rotation'') makes a root-level live capture terminal.
* Social-recovery wallets confirm our own canon (`civic-recovery` keel: "recovery quorum IS the impersonation quorum"). Buterin, verbatim: ''"a majority [of guardians] can cooperate to change the signing key of the account"'' (https://vitalik.eth.limo/general/2021/01/11/recovery.html). Argent, Safe, Buterin all fall back to the same non-cryptographic levers — guardian diversity/anonymity + a time-lock+veto window.

''EXPOSURE (what the field ships that we have ruled but not shaped).'' The ''time-lock + veto window is the ONLY lever that touches a genuinely live key'', and it is a first-class, ''deployed'' primitive everywhere our layered recovery only names it:

* did:plc: priority-ordered rotation keys + a ''72-hour window'' in which a ''higher-authority'' (colder, socially/offline-held) rotation key ''rewrites history, clobbering any operations signed by a lower-authority key'' (https://web.plc.directory/spec/v0.1/did-plc). This is our Fork-C (threshold + time-lock + veto) made concrete and running at Bluesky scale: a defector rotates with the seized lower-authority key; the victim's cold high-authority key clobbers within the window.
* Argent `recoveryPeriod` 36h; Safe 28-day default; Buterin's 1-week time-locked vault (owner can cancel during the week).
* Nostr NIP-41 (draft): pre-committed successor key, OpenTimestamp-anchored, with a ''30-day public contest window'' (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nostr-protocol/nips/nip41/41.md) — a rosterless witness (OpenTimestamps) + a challenge window, solving exactly what SSB gave up.

''NEGENTROPY TO ADOPT.''

# A ''priority/authority ladder of rotation keys + a bounded rewrite window'', landing in `recovery-registration` and the handle-KEL rotate verb: the armed self-recovery digest we already incept (`deriveSelfRecoveryKey`) becomes a ''higher-authority'' key that can supersede a live-key rotation inside a window the sensorium opens on detection. This is precisely the operator's standing lean — ''pull recovery-quorum forward beside the sensorium'' — given a shape.
# ''Proactive Secret Sharing folded into the HandleGlamour graft.'' FROST (RFC 9591) is signing-only — ''"Key generation for FROST signing is out of scope"'' (https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9591) — but PSS (Herzberg et al., CRYPTO '95) and its deployments (Zcash Foundation `frost` #245; Fireblocks refreshing shares at ''minute intervals'', https://eprint.iacr.org/2020/492; CHURP for dynamic committees) refresh shares at an epoch boundary so a defector's captured share ''expires next epoch, public key unchanged''. Map: our "rolling current set / graft" already rotates membership; make the graft ''also'' a share-refresh so a turned cabal-member's share dies at the next roll. This binds our epoch-as-monotone-frontier (RANK 3) directly to the live-defector case.

''ANTI-PATTERN.'' Duress schemes teach the trap by contrast: GrapheneOS duress-wipe, LUKS-nuke, VeraCrypt hidden volumes, Canarytokens all ''destroy or signal'' — none rotate an ''already-copied'' key, and all fall to the observation/suppression problem (coercer images first, watches the signal, blocks the channel). Do NOT build a "duress key" believing it recovers you; it only denies future access or raises an alarm. The residual is inherent, not a shortfall to engineer away.

''Folds into:'' `live-equivocation.mem` #owed (the whole recovery-field survey answers questions 1); `recovery-ruling-layered` + `recovery-registration` (the window + authority-ladder shape); a note in `field-collision.mem` #standing-tensions that the field CONFIRMS the residual is universal.

