<<~ ahu #/rank-2-watchers>>

!! RANK 2 — The OWED watcher layer (equivocation detection is carriage) — and its near-twin exists

`field-collision.mem` left watchers OWED: a per-reader view catches a lying Handle only if readers can COMPARE views. Two systems have built exactly this, ledger-free, and one is almost our design.

''VINDICATION + the strongest single find: did:webvh.'' It is the ONLY system in the survey that pairs ''ledger-free pre-rotation'' (`nextKeyHashes` — commit the ''hash'' of your next authorized key, so a stolen current key cannot seize succession — identical in spirit to our `nextHandleKeyDigest`) ''WITH an in-protocol witness+watcher layer'': ''witnesses'' threshold-gate updates (`did-witness.json`); ''watchers'' are non-voting monitors that cache the DID Log and ''detect equivocation'' (https://identity.foundation/didwebvh/v1.0/). It also gives credible exit via `portable: true` + `alsoKnownAs` while the SCID (self-certifying id) survives a full host move. This is a near-twin of our handle-KEL + Meshpalace-watcher + severability design, arrived at independently — strong negentropy that we are on a real attractor.

''KERI supplies the role vocabulary, fully specified.'' Watcher (keeps a KEL it is not a designated witness of) -> ''Juror'' (performs duplicity detection, keeps mutually-inconsistent versions) -> ''Jury'' (fault-tolerant juror pool) -> ''Judge'' (evaluates on juror evidence), under ''"first seen, always seen, never unseen"'', and watchers ''"should share notes with each other"'' = gossip (https://rufftimo.medium.com/keri-101-witnesses-watchers-detectability-fb604cae7a26). This is a deployed-spec blueprint for our unbuilt Meshpalace sensorium (`field-collision.mem` #the-coniks-resolution names its home but says the palace is unbuilt).

''SSB gives the free intrinsic detector:'' each message hashes `previous`+`sequence`, so a fork is cryptographically self-incriminating — a witness-free equivocation detector baked into the log shape (https://ssbc.github.io/scuttlebutt-protocol-guide/). Our KEL already has this shape.

''EXPOSURE.'' The newer local-first stacks we rhyme with — ''Willow, Iroh, Veilid, DXOS, UCAN — all LACK a witness/equivocation layer'' and push it up to the application. So our owed watcher is genuinely under-provided by the field; we cannot pull it from Keyhive/Iroh/Willow. Only did:webvh + KERI + CONIKS solve it. did:plc admits its central directory can still misorder a fork and is ''moving toward an append-only transparency log "similar to certificate transparency"'' (https://github.com/did-method-plc/did-method-plc) — i.e. the field is converging on exactly the CONIKS/watcher layer we owe.

''NEGENTROPY TO ADOPT.'' Adopt did:webvh's ''witness-threshold-gates-an-update ⊥ non-voting-watcher-archives-and-alarms'' split as the Meshpalace sensorium's two roles, named with KERI's juror/jury/judge + first-seen-always-seen. Adopt ''RIBLT/range-based set reconciliation'' (Keyhive's Beelay uses Rateless IBLT; Willow uses fingerprint-then-subdivide) as the head-sighting gossip transport — it catches a forked KEL head far cheaper than naive head-gossip on drifted stores (the extension `field-collision.mem` #the-mesh-field already flagged for Willow RBSR, now doubly confirmed).

''ANTI-PATTERN.'' UCAN ships ''eventually-consistent revocation with no witness layer'' — an agent holding an ''alternate'' valid proof chain keeps access despite revocation, and the burden lands on every verifier's cache freshness (https://github.com/ucan-wg/revocation). Do not let our capability revocation (kapae/antigen) rely on cache-freshness without the watcher gossiping the contradiction.

''Folds into:'' `field-collision.mem` #the-coniks-resolution (did:webvh as the shipped twin; KERI juror/jury/judge vocabulary; the field-wide gap confirming the watcher is load-bearing); the Meshpalace/`dreamnet-architecture` design.

