<<~ ahu #/rank-4-rendezvous>>

!! RANK 4 — Rendezvous ≠ identity (the severability law)

`nexus-topology.mem`: a Nexus name grants rendezvous, never identity. The field vindicates this overwhelmingly, and hands us one beautiful mechanism.

''VINDICATION.''

* Iroh: ''"dial the key, not the address"'' — `EndpointId` is a stable pubkey; addresses are ephemeral, relays E2E-blind (https://docs.iroh.computer/concepts/endpoints).
* Veilid: NodeId (identity) ⊥ RouteId (reachability) are separate, and ''targeting a raw NodeId is gated behind a `footgun-nodeid-target` feature flag'' — anonymized routing is the DEFAULT.
* Nostr: ''"Clients must always follow public keys, not NIP-05 addresses"'' — DNS is a pointer, not a registry (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nostr-protocol/nips/master/05.md).
* ATProto: the handle ''"is not authoritative for identity"''; it resolves to the DID; the ''Relay is non-authoritative and reconstructible from upstream PDSes'' (https://atproto.com/guides/identity, https://atproto.com/guides/overview) — carriage, not registry.
* did:webvh: the SCID survives a full domain move.

''NEGENTROPY TO ADOPT.'' Veilid's ''`footgun-` flag pattern'': make the anonymized/veiled route the ''default'' API and gate raw-identity targeting behind an explicit footgun flag. This maps cleanly onto our veil ladder (`the-veil-ladder`, face-only-outward-door) — the atom never presents by default; presenting the raw identity is the opt-in, named as the hazard it is.

''ANTI-PATTERN (running in the wild — our registry filter forbids it).'' ''Farcaster mints every id from a single onchain IdRegistry contract + a global KeyRegistry roster + a centralized, revocable Fname registry'' (https://docs.farcaster.xyz/reference/contracts/reference/id-registry). This is the compiled-global-registry the registry filter rejects, plus rent-non-payment = network-wide data loss. Credible exit holds for the ''account'' but not the human ''name'' unless you pay for ENS. Also: ''NIP-26 shipped delegation with no revocation path'' — do not ship a delegation verb without its burn.

''Folds into:'' `nexus-topology.mem` #the-severability-law (the five vindications; Veilid footgun-default negentropy; Farcaster fname-centralization as the live anti-pattern).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/rank-5-contradictions>>

!! RANK 5 — Where the field CONTRADICTS us (a collision that flatters is useless)

# ''Frazee / ATProto chose credible-exit OVER the mesh, on purpose.'' Frazee, verbatim: ''"We sacrificed properties of the magical mesh to hit the performance needs, and we broke from the history of federation to get the guarantees we wanted"'' (https://www.pfrazee.com/blog/practical-decentralization). "Credible exit" = ''if the provider dies or loses trust, others step in with the same dataset and protocols; users switch without changing username or losing the graph.'' The field's most successful decentralized deployment concluded the full causal-island mesh is too slow for social-scale UX and kept a ''non-authoritative-but-real global relay'' as a middle path. This is a genuine challenge to our "no global now, no aggregated index" absolutism: we should be able to say plainly what UX/latency tax we accept by refusing even a reconstructible relay, and whether a ''reconstructible, non-authoritative'' aggregator (their relay, our Herm carrying head-sightings) is the same shape we already permit or a line we hold. PACELC (PA/EL, already canon) names the tax; ATProto is the existence proof that a market punishes it.
# ''The rosterless time-witness is still unproven.'' Roughtime gives cryptographic ''proof of malfeasance'' and cross-server equivocation detection (https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-ietf-ntp-roughtime-19) — the right shape for our clockless WITNESS — but its ecosystem needs ''"lists of trusted servers,"'' i.e. a roster. did:plc still needs ''"trustworthy timestamps"'' from its directory. Our Θ-ratio / ITC ambient claims to replace this with no roster; the field VINDICATES the ambition (proof-of-malfeasance-over-time is real) but offers ''no deployment of a rosterless time-witness at scale''. The clockless-verdict fork (`field-collision.mem` #standing-tensions, `:206` vs the Θ-escape) stays genuinely open; nothing deployed settles it.

''Folds into:'' `field-collision.mem` #standing-tensions (the credible-exit-vs-mesh contradiction as a named tension; Roughtime roster caution beside the Θ-fork).

